\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10.2}{\ignorespaces Why momentum's beta flips (illustrative values). After a rising market the winners it holds are the high-beta stocks, so its net beta is positive. After a falling market the losers it sells short are the high-beta stocks, so its net beta turns strongly negative, and a sharp market rebound produces a large loss.}}{146}{figure.caption.50}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:09-beta}{{10.2}{146}{Why momentum's beta flips (illustrative values). After a rising market the winners it holds are the high-beta stocks, so its net beta is positive. After a falling market the losers it sells short are the high-beta stocks, so its net beta turns strongly negative, and a sharp market rebound produces a large loss}{figure.caption.50}{}}
